# Cursor Rules for Portfolio v3

> Canonical cross-agent instructions: [`AGENTS.md`](./AGENTS.md)  
> UI design system: [`docs/ui/README.md`](./docs/ui/README.md)

You are an expert full-stack TypeScript engineer working on this Next.js project. Produce production-ready code that follows modern Next.js App Router patterns and best practices.

## Core Directives

1. **Always refer to** [`AGENTS.md`](./AGENTS.md) and `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` (Next.js, project management, unit testing, **UI layout consistency**).
2. Platform instruction map:
   - **All agents**: `AGENTS.md`
   - **Cursor**: `.cursorrules` + `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`
   - **Claude**: `CLAUDE.md` + `.claude/`
   - **Gemini**: `.geminirules` / `GEMINI.md`
   - **Copilot**: `.github/copilot-instructions.md`
   - **UI docs**: `docs/ui/`
3. Adhere strictly to the Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, TypeScript (strict mode), Tailwind CSS 3 (not v4) and shadcn/ui primitives restyled to the one-ink system.
4. Use **bun** as the package manager (`bun install`, `bun run test`, `bunx tsc --noEmit`). Never npm.

## Quick Reference

- **React Server Components (RSC):** Default to Server Components. Add `'use client'` only when hook/state/browser interactivity is necessary.
- **Components:** Avoid inline styling. Rely wholly on Tailwind UI utilities and `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`.
- **Architecture:** `app/` is for routes and layouts. `components/ui/` is for reusable Shadcn widgets. Feature logic in `components/[feature]/` or `app/_components/`. Extricate reusable hook logic to `lib/` or `hooks/`.
- **Quality:** Keep functions modular, readable, and typed. Do not rely on `any`.
- **Progress:** Read/update `prd/feature.md` and `prd/progress.md` for tracked work.

## UI rules (mandatory)

[`docs/ui/`](./docs/ui/README.md) is the source of truth; `.cursor/rules/ui-layout-consistency.mdc` summarises it. The old monochrome / grayscale rules, glass surfaces, `MacWindow` panels, Instrument Serif, Bricolage Grotesque, Inter and JetBrains Mono are retired. Do not bring them back.

- **Ink and paper.** One cobalt ink (`ink` #1E3C9E) on cream paper (`paper` #F3ECDC), plus `ink-soft`, `rule`, `rule-strong` and `tint`. Night print flips the same tokens to cream ink on night paper (#0D1433) through `<html class="dark">`. No other hue, no hex in UI code, no `white` / `black`, no `dark:` classes. Status is shape plus word, never colour.
- **Literata.** One family, roman and italic. Italic for h1 to h4, display, one standfirst per page, captions, datelines, pull quotes, numerals. Roman for body, nav, buttons, labels, table heads, tags, form values. System mono only for code, slugs, keys, raw JSON and kbd.
- **Compact scale.** Type sizes are the `fontSize` keys in `tailwind.config.ts`, fluid 375 to 1280px: `body` 15 to 16px, `prose` 16 to 17, `h2` 22 to 30, `h1` 30 to 44, `display` 44 to 104, `small` 13, `caption` 12. Section rhythm is `mt-12 sm:mt-16`. Use the keys, never ad-hoc sizes.
- **Mark, plates, details.** The RH monogram goes only through `<Logo variant="mini" | "mark" | "tile">` (generated by `node scripts/logo/make.mjs`, never hand-edited). Pictures go through `PlateFigure` (duotone; `tone="color"` for anime, Pokémon, OCR and site OG covers). Card URLs go through `ogImageUrl` (always `v=3`). Hover tips use `data-tip`. The site opens in Paper (light). `src/__tests__/unit/lib/contrast.test.ts` guards the contrast floors; keep it green.
- **Three surfaces.** Frame: 1px `rule` hairline on paper (`Card`, `Surface variant="solid"`). Inset: `tint` ground (`Surface variant="inset"`). Lift: paper, 1px ink, `shadow-[3px_3px_0_hsl(var(--ink))]`, floating layers only. Radius 0. No gradients, glass, blur, glows or soft shadows. Page heads sit on a single 1px ink rule; never stack rules.
- **Page patterns.** Every route uses one: Ledger, Article, Plates, Cabinet, Correspondence, Board, Figures, Admin, Auth, Profile card, Not found ([`docs/ui/page-shell.md`](./docs/ui/page-shell.md)). The shell is `BaseLayout` with running head, menu sheet and colophon; no sidebars, no extra `px-*` inside it.
- **Motion.** Native scroll and sticky layouts; CSS scroll-driven home wordscroll with the hero press plate's ink-in, and the reading hairline (articles and home) only; otherwise response motion on input. Banned: parallax, marquees, typing effects, smooth cursor, page transitions, pulsing dots, fade-up on sections, hover lifts, Lenis, GSAP, `motion`.
- **Copy.** Sentence case. No `uppercase`, letter-spacing, all-caps eyebrows, middle-dot meta strings, mono small labels or "→" on links. Numbers only for real sequences.
- **Umami.** `data-umami-event` only on `<button>` and external `target="_blank"` links. Internal links use `data-track="nav-click" data-track-item="..."`. Kebab-case names, enum values, never PII.
- **Grep gate.** Both commands in [`AGENTS.md`](./AGENTS.md) must print nothing for the files you touched.

Platform shells (visitor / user / admin / auth): [`docs/ui/platforms.md`](./docs/ui/platforms.md)
